                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Low quality porn disguised as a low quality FPS.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/O2PmXR0TkY0\n\nI was hesitant to do this game based on the... 'feature set' that was advertised. My fears were proven to be fairly accurate.\n\nExperiment Gone Rogue, also known as 10 Cupcakes, puts you in the shoes of a human super soldier genetically altered by aliens pretending to be benevolent rulers of Earth. It's a decent enough setup if we ignore the fact that humans wouldn't just let an alien race take over regardless of how nice they were.\n\nYou run through a variety of levels while escaping fighting 3 types of enemies. The males that blindly rush you to get in a fist fight. The ledge riflemen that are never on the same level as you and peppering you with energy rounds. Finally the \"Valkyries\" or the female, armored, sword wielders. This was the extent of the \"Varied Enemies\" bullet point. There were unique boss fights that were fairly interesting however the levels themselves had 0 variety.\n\nThere were destructible objects in the game but they offered nothing to the gameplay.\n\nGraphically I wasn't really impressed either. It wasn't outright bad but it wasn't quite good either. Mediocre.\n\nGame mechanics like grabbing rockets or grenades were beholden to the same grip setting as the weapons making them fairly difficult to throw well. As this was supposed to be a key part of boss fights it just added frustration. You're forced to choose between a throwing mechanic that makes sense and having to hold grip to keep your weapon in your hand. That gets really old, really quick. These should have been two separate options.\n\nThe climbing portion of the game wasn't bad. Even including some secret areas to find weapon upgrades. Standard Climby mechanics.\n\nThe flow of the game felt very stunted. The long winded story booths were oddly positioned in the levels such that you could go a while without getting one or you could have several back to back with little to no combat between. They were poorly placed had me feeling like I just wanted to move on already. I love story in my games but these felt like a chore I HAD to do rather than information I WANTED to listen to.\n\nOverall the FPS side of things felt like minimal effort was put into the game.\n\nThe Go Go Bar.\n\nSo we've discussed the poorly made FPS wrapper. Time to discuss the nougat center? Hmmm, not quite.\n\nThe bar offers scantily clad women dancing on stage for you to oogle. A quick lever pull and they drop their clothes to both topless and fully nude options. There is an unlockable VIP party room that has many girls dancing on the floor in a group. You also can pick any stage dancer to give you a lapdance.\n\nThe performance as soon as you walk in takes a dip. If you go into the VIP room, prepare for nausea as you drop to 15-20 FPS. The bar is very poorly optimized.\n\nLapdances lock you into position over the lapdance chair with access to a button that changes the dancer. This button only works once and for some reason when you push it, your current dancer falls to her death through a trap door.... You're able to slap the dancer on her side to change her animation. There are 3 animations and she does have voice lines but these also repeat very quickly.\n\nHopefully you were ready to quite the game when you started the dance because there's no way to quit the dance after it's started other than exiting to the menu.\n\nThis game fails as a shooter and it fails as porn.",
